Question,Answer
Tell me about a recent project you are proud of and your role in it.,"Choose a project where you can clearly explain your own part, such as a final year project, an internship task or a personal app. Describe the problem, the technologies you used, what you personally did, and the result. Personal projects outside class are a big plus because they show passion for IT."
Tell me about a time you could not solve a problem. What did you do?,"Be honest about the situation and what blocked you. Then explain your next steps, such as searching documentation, asking a senior or teammate, or escalating the issue properly. Interviewers want to see that you stay calm, find help, and learn from it."
How do you deal with deadlines?,"Explain how you plan your work, for example by breaking a project into small tasks with their own dates and checking your progress often. Give an example of a tight deadline you met. If a deadline was ever missed, explain how you informed the team early and what you changed afterwards."
What preparations do you do before starting a project?,"Explain your steps, such as understanding the requirements, asking questions, researching suitable tools, planning tasks and setting up version control like Git. Mention whether you plan alone or with the team. This shows you are organised and do not just jump straight into coding."
Why did you decide to go into IT?,"Explain what genuinely attracts you to IT, such as solving problems, building things with code, or always learning something new. Give a short real example, like the first program or website you made. Then link that interest to why you want this particular role."
How do you stay up to date with new technology?,"Mention the real ways you keep learning, such as online courses, tech blogs, YouTube channels, newsletters, podcasts or tech communities. Give one recent thing you learned. This shows you are curious and will keep improving."
What would you do if you were in charge of the whole organisation’s technology?,"Show that you can think beyond your own tasks. Share a simple vision, such as improving security, moving systems to the cloud or automating manual work, and explain how you would plan it step by step. This shows leadership potential and a growth mindset."
"What do you think is the most pressing problem in tech today, and how would you fix it?","Pick one issue you understand well, such as cybersecurity threats, data privacy or the misuse of AI. Explain why it matters to people and businesses, then suggest a clear and realistic solution. This shows big-picture thinking and problem-solving skills."
What is your troubleshooting process?,"Use clear steps: first identify the problem and ask questions, then find the cause, test a possible fix, confirm the problem is solved, and finally document what happened. Give a simple example, such as fixing a user’s internet connection."
What is an IP address?,"An IP address is a unique number given to every device on a network, such as a laptop or phone, like a home address for computers. It lets devices find and send data to each other over the internet or a local network. An IPv4 address looks like 192.168.1.10."
